
auth {
  mode: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{token}}
}

docs {
  # Thing-Tag API

  1. Select the **Local** environment (top-right).
  2. Run **01 Auth / Login** first - it stores the JWT in the `token` runtime variable,
     which every other request sends via collection-level Bearer auth.
  3. Event lists (/api/TrackingEvents) use cursor paging: pass `nextCursor` back as
     `?cursor=`; add `includeTotalCount=true` only when a total is needed.
  4. Or run the whole collection with the Runner (folders in order): requests are
     chained through runtime variables (ids created earlier are reused later) and
     codes include a per-run `runId`, so the collection can be re-run against the
     same database.

  The Shipments folder walks a full multimodal journey:
  Bangkok hub -> (truck) -> Laem Chabang port -> (vessel) -> Tokyo port -> (van) -> customer,
  including a customs hold/clear and final delivery.
}
